% Exactness in causal inference: from conjugate/forward-exact inference to
% efficient estimation with confidence-interval guarantees.
%
% Two senses of "exact" run through this list:
%   Sense 1 (forward-exact) -- closed-form conditional/interventional LAWS
%     from a fully specified DGP: conjugacy, Gaussian/discrete graphical
%     inference, and symbolic do-calculus identification. Sections A-C.
%   Sense 2 (efficient estimation) -- estimating a causal functional from
%     DATA with the smallest variance and a valid confidence interval:
%     semiparametric efficiency, EIF, DML, TMLE, auto-debiasing, GMM.
%     Sections D-I.
% Plus partial identification (J) for when point ID fails, and
% finite-sample-exact randomization inference (K).
%
% Compiled for Nudagitty. Titles double-braced to preserve capitalization.

